Here are the limits of each function at $x=0$, according to the graphs:

$\begin{align}
&\blueD{\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}g(x)=-1}
\\\\
&\maroonD{\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}h(x)=0}
\end{align}$

Now we can find $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}\Big(g(x)-h(x)\Big)$ using the fact that the limit of a difference of functions is the difference of the individual limits:

$\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}\Big(g(x)-h(x)\Big)=\lim_{x\to 0}g(x)-\lim_{x\to 0}h(x)$
